          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef multinomial_nb_lidstone_prob(counts_c0, counts_c1, x_doc, prior_c1: float, alpha: float = 1.0) -> float:\n    c0 = np.asarray(counts_c0, dtype=float)\n    c1 = np.asarray(counts_c1, dtype=float)\n    x = np.asarray(x_doc, dtype=float)\n    V = len(c0)\n    th0 = (c0 + alpha) / (np.sum(c0) + alpha * V)\n    th1 = (c1 + alpha) / (np.sum(c1) + alpha * V)\n    lp0 = np.log(1.0 - prior_c1) + float(x @ np.log(th0))\n    lp1 = np.log(prior_c1) + float(x @ np.log(th1))\n    m = max(lp0, lp1)\n    p1 = float(np.exp(lp1 - (m + np.log(np.exp(lp0 - m) + np.exp(lp1 - m)))))\n    return round(p1, 4)\n```"
